        "thinking": "The errors are coming from the db package, not from our CF package files. These errors exist because the CF package's tsconfig has `rootDir: \"../../\"` so it ends up including files from the db package too. Let me look at what's included in our tsconfig and find if there's a way to scope the type-checking properly.\n\nThe issue is that:\n1. `rootDir: \"../../\"` is needed so that relative imports from `server/src/` work\n2. But with the CF tsconfig's `include: [\"src/**/*.ts\"]`, it only checks CF src files\n3. However TypeScript will also type-check files that are imported by those included files, transitively\n\n\n4. When CF imports from `@paperclipai/db`, TypeScript tries to type-check those db files, but the db package's dependencies like `postgres` and `drizzle-orm` aren't installed in the CF package's node_modules—they're only in the db package's node_modules.\n\nI need to check if `postgres` is actually listed in the CF package's dependencies, and then look at what errors are showing up specifically in the CF source files themselves.",
